  "notes": "Event affects two units (Unit 1 and Unit 3) simultaneously via a common transformer fault; both Unit and Unit3 nodes created and OCCURRED_AT linked. No BACKED_UP_BY edge asserted for redundant A-train/B-train buses since they were not part of the failed chain but rather unaffected parallel trains — captured narratively in chain summary instead, per rule 6's requirement that backups be explicitly stated as operable during the inoperability window (the redundant buses were never inoperable, so the affected buses' 'backup' was restoration via alternate transformer, captured as corrective action, not a System backup edge). Previous-similar-event LER numbers not stated in narrative (only month/year and cause given) so key set to 'unknown' per lack of an explicit LER number; plant/unit/title captured per rule 9."
